Author: aquinas-bot <aquinasbot@proton.me>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 13:44:29 2026 +0000

    psi: keep helper-returned views usable across calls that may pause (#1672)
    
    * psi: retain evaluated sources of returned field views
    
    A helper returning a field view must keep the reference that supplied that field. Record its exact descriptor capture, descriptor path and new referent suffix separately from pointer-forwarding associations. Crossing a stored reference uses the invocation-entry snapshot; inline actuals keep their own completion.
    
    Intermediate checkpoint only: resource authentication and formation wiring are next, with no repaired execution claim. Exact optimized e461 baseline accepts and runs the direct probe but rejects helper-returned, no-recast and inline-source probes for missing retained lifetime. Nine-place inputs and policy twins are frozen; the constant-place authoring correction is recorded separately before compiler edits.
    
    * psi: authenticate borrowing parents of helper field views
    
    Distinguish forwarding a returned descriptor from forming a new returned projection. The latter keeps the completed actual, its presented access, nearest real borrowing parent and original whole-input debt. Every body-selected source must have a matching checked formation; explicit argument borrows use their real call access rather than a named-local requirement.
    
    Resource authentication consumes the new evaluated-source relation without treating pointer geometry or lifetime signatures as authority. This is an unqualified implementation checkpoint before the first optimized repair producer and focused source/runtime checks.
    
    * psi: compare complete returned-view source identities
    
    Use the same full captured-place equality for represented alternatives and the selected formation, including incoming reference identity and its owner path. Preserve the first candidate as unqualified diagnostic evidence; add focused refusal context to resolve its selected-source correspondence gap.
    
    * psi: keep lending sources distinct from call input debt
    
    Follow each formed argument to its exact evaluated reference boundary before finding its lending loan. Stored-source failure stays unavailable; only a genuine argument formation or captured incoming association can request the checked CallAccess grant. Complete call input debt remains separate. Share address-capture queries with ordinary view formation.
    
    Classify readable mutable reference slots by their current declared view. Existing lowering rebinds that home on assignment, so the replacement read and a surviving saved view can retain different pointers. Read/write authority and frozen-content checks remain separate.
    
    * psi: report exact projected-source lookup refusals
    
    Retain a diagnostic checkpoint distinguishing unavailable frozen inventories, missing binding predecessors, source type disagreement and unmatched formation occurrences. Compare projected source prototypes to the actual published call operands. No permission or fallback change; this trace is temporary investigation evidence.
    
    * psi: preserve checked sources of projected call views
    
    * psi: use canonical captures for output lifetime inputs
    
    * psi: follow every saved descriptor to its actual borrow
    
    * psi: pin returned-view carry through all nine places
    
    * psi: retain projected sources without inventing absolute addresses
    
    * psi: authenticate returned roots in their invocation namespace
    
    * psi: bind independent identity to its returned formation path
    
    * psi: retain captured byte storage when a helper returns an element
    
    * psi: keep source refusal reasons without diagnostic tracing
    
    * psi: report the structural projection that execution cannot resolve
    
    * psi: limit refusal context changes to the affected boundary
    
    * psi: match exact byte return coordinates against captured storage
    
    * psi: separate retained byte descriptors from owned value observations
    
    * psi: pin projected image return compatibility and execution
    
    * psi: supply exact crash summaries in constant-scope test data
    
    * psi: explain saved view permissions before internal records
    
    * test: declare storage used by capability graph returns
    
    * psi: follow saved whole-reference results to their suppliers
    
    * psi: record helper-returned view execution and rejection oracles
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Zachary Canann <zcanann@Zacharys-Mac-mini.local>

